{
  "title": "CHAPTER 3: SECTORS OF THE ECONOMY",
  "order": 2,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "82opgxk",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. MEANING OF ECONOMIC ACTIVITIES"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Economic activities are undertaken to earn income through the production, distribution, and exchange of goods and services.",
        "The primary sector involves direct extraction of natural resources, while the secondary sector converts raw materials into finished goods.",
        "The tertiary (service) sector is the largest contributor to India's GDP, contributing around 50–55%.",
        "India experienced rapid service-led growth following the 1991 Economic Reforms.",
        "In disguised unemployment, common in agriculture, removing extra workers does not decrease total production because their marginal productivity is zero."
      ],
      "id": "odhrfyq"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Agriculture GDP",
          "value": "15–17%",
