    {
      "id": "716n4h5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "STRUCTURAL TRANSFORMATION THROUGH PLANS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "India's planning strategy gradually shifted the economy from agriculture-dominated to industry-focused and eventually to service-led growth.",
      "id": "c9c9rsr"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Early Plans → Agriculture focus<br/>• Mid Plans → Industrial expansion<br/>• Post-1991 → Service sector boom<br/>",
      "id": "nrpj69h"
    },
    {
      "id": "goppdy2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. SECTOR CONTRIBUTION TO GDP (INDIA)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Agriculture – Around 15–17%<br/>• Industry – Around 28–30%<br/>• Services – Around 50–55%",
      "id": "yflz7hb"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Agriculture employs large population but contributes less to GDP.",
      "id": "opbrsgb"
    },
