    {
      "id": "p40vzn8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "12.DISGUISED UNEMPLOYMENT"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Meaning:<br/>Disguised unemployment refers to a situation where more people are employed than actually required for a given level of output. If some workers are removed, total production does not decrease. In such cases, marginal productivity of additional workers is zero.",
      "id": "4rg33s4"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "In disguised unemployment, the marginal productivity of additional workers is always zero.",
        "The Tertiary Sector constitutes the maximum share (50–55%) of India's GDP, while the Primary Sector employs the most workers.",
        "Post-1991 Economic Reforms triggered India's rapid transition from an agriculture-dominated to a service-led economy."
      ],
      "id": "we3gf5t"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Example:<br/>Suppose a farm requires only 4 workers to produce 100 units of wheat, but 8 workers are working on the same farm. Even if 3–4 workers leave, output remains 100 units. This means extra workers were not contributing to production.",
      "id": "uebeni7"
    },
    {
      "id": "93h8mog",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Characteristics of Disguised Unemployment"
    },
    {
      "id": "uo4ulhv",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Feature</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Explanation</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Hidden Unemployment</p>",
            "<p>Workers appear employed but are not productive</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Zero Marginal Productivity</p>",
            "<p>Removing extra workers does not reduce output</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Common in Agriculture</p>",
            "<p>Mostly found in rural farming areas</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Low Productivity</p>",
            "<p>Output per worker remains low</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Causes:<br/>• Population pressure on land<br/>• Small land holdings<br/>• Lack of industrial jobs<br/>• Lack of skill diversification",
      "id": "k1dd9jp"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Effects:<br/>• Low income per capita<br/>• Poverty<br/>• Inefficient use of labour<br/>• Slower economic growth",
      "id": "kqd9qru"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Solutions:<br/>• Industrialisation<br/>• Skill development<br/>• Rural employment schemes<br/>• Diversification of rural economy",
      "id": "jqowyad"
    },
    {
